solnix: xhci -- warm-reset a USB 3 root port whose link did not train (SS.Inactive / Compliance / Cold Attach
Status), so a device plugged in before boot is enumerated, as Linux and FreeBSD do.

WHY
- Measured on the X1 Extreme Gen5 (r1 image, 2026-10-21): a Belkin RTL8153 (USB 3, 5 Gb/s) on a left USB-C port,
  whose SuperSpeed lines are on the Thunderbolt 4 xHCI 56:00.0 (8086:1138 Maple Ridge), was NOT seen when plugged
  in before boot ("no wired NIC"). After an unplug/replug, usbecm0 came up at 1 Gb/s. So the controller, hubd and
  the driver work, and only the device present at controller reset is missed.
- MECHANISM (candidate, from the specs and two other OSes; NOT yet read off the X1E's registers): xHCI 1.2 5.4.8
  and 4.19.1.2.4.1: a USB 3 device attached when the port powers up can fail link training. The port then reports
  PLS = SS.Inactive (6) or Compliance (10), often with PORTSC.CAS (Cold Attach Status) set, and CCS clear. Only a
  warm reset (PORTSC.WPR) leaves that state. A hot-plug trains normally, which matches the replug result.
- illumos neither sees nor fixes that state. xhci_hub.c's GET_STATUS translation ignores CAS and the link state,
  so hubd sees no connection, and hubd never issues a warm reset. Linux 6.12 xhci-hub.c
  xhci_hub_report_usb3_link_state reports CONNECTION for CAS (as Compliance), and hub.c
  hub_port_warm_reset_required() turns the port reset of an SS.Inactive/Compliance port into BH_PORT_RESET.
  FreeBSD usb_hub.c warm-resets SS_INA (usbd_req_warm_reset_port, usb_request.c: U3/COMP/LOOPBACK/SS_INA).

THE CHANGE (xhci_hub.c only; hubd's own reset/enumerate path is unchanged)
- xhci_port_needs_warm_reset(raw PORTSC): port powered, and CAS set or PLS SS.Inactive/Compliance.
- GET_STATUS reports such a port as connected (PORT_STATUS_CCS), so hubd's attach-time scan
  (hubd_determine_port_connection) and its hotplug thread call hubd_handle_port_connect.
- SET_FEATURE(PORT_RESET) on such a port sets WPR instead of PR. hubd already waits for the reset change and
  clears C_BH_PORT_RESET (hubdi.c hubd_reset_port). One system-log NOTE ("!", not the console) per warm
  reset with the raw PORTSC.
- Tunable xhci_ss_warm_reset (default 1). 0 is the old behaviour, which is the negative control.
RUNG: compiles with the gate's warning set, and is modelled under KVM with a QEMU qemu-xhci patched to hold a
present-at-boot SuperSpeed device in SS.Inactive with CAS until a warm reset. NOT measured on the X1E; the
solnix-diag PORTSC dump (/usr/lib/xhci/xhci_portsc) is what shows whether the X1E's port is in that state.

--- a/usr/src/uts/common/io/usb/hcd/xhci/xhci_hub.c
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/io/usb/hcd/xhci/xhci_hub.c
@@ -22,6 +22,34 @@
 #include <sys/usb/hcd/xhci/xhci.h>
 
 /*
+ * A USB 3 device that is already plugged in when the controller is reset can
+ * fail link training: the port then sits in SS.Inactive or Compliance, often
+ * with Cold Attach Status (CAS) set and CCS clear, and only a warm reset
+ * trains it (xHCI 1.2 4.19.1.2, 5.4.8). Hot-plug trains normally, so such a
+ * device is seen only after a replug. hubd knows nothing of warm resets, so
+ * report such a port as connected and turn hubd's port reset into a warm
+ * one, as Linux does (xhci_hub_report_usb3_link_state: CAS or Compliance ->
+ * connected; hub_port_warm_reset_required) and FreeBSD does (uhub on SS_INA
+ * -> usbd_req_warm_reset_port). Set to 0 for the old behaviour.
+ */
+uint_t xhci_ss_warm_reset = 1;
+
+#define	XHCI_PLS_SS_INACTIVE	6
+#define	XHCI_PLS_COMPLIANCE	10
+
+/* reg is a raw PORTSC read */
+static boolean_t
+xhci_port_needs_warm_reset(uint32_t reg)
+{
+	uint_t pls = XHCI_PS_PLS_GET(reg);
+
+	if (xhci_ss_warm_reset == 0 || !(reg & XHCI_PS_PP))
+		return (B_FALSE);
+	return ((reg & XHCI_PS_CAS) != 0 || pls == XHCI_PLS_SS_INACTIVE ||
+	    pls == XHCI_PLS_COMPLIANCE);
+}
+
+/*
  * The following structure and global define the default configuration that we
  * 'deliver' to USBA on behalf of our hub. However, it's worth noting that it's
  * going to take this in as an array of bytes off of the wire, whereas we're
@@ -325,7 +353,7 @@
 	int feat = ucrp->ctrl_wValue;
 	int port = XHCI_PS_INDPORT(ucrp->ctrl_wIndex);
 	uint32_t val = XHCI_PS_INDVAL(ucrp->ctrl_wIndex);
-	uint32_t reg;
+	uint32_t reg, raw;
 	uintptr_t index;
 
 	ASSERT(MUTEX_HELD(&xhcip->xhci_lock));
@@ -336,7 +364,7 @@
 		return (USB_CR_UNSPECIFIED_ERR);
 
 	index = XHCI_PORTSC(port);
-	reg = xhci_get32(xhcip, XHCI_R_OPER, index);
+	reg = raw = xhci_get32(xhcip, XHCI_R_OPER, index);
 	if (xhci_check_regs_acc(xhcip) != DDI_FM_OK) {
 		xhci_error(xhcip, "failed to read port status register for "
 		    "port %d: encountered fatal FM error, resetting device",
@@ -404,7 +432,15 @@
 		reg |= XHCI_PS_WPR;
 		break;
 	case CFS_PORT_RESET:
-		reg |= XHCI_PS_PR;
+		if (xhci_port_needs_warm_reset(raw)) {
+			xhci_log(xhcip, "!port %d: USB 3 link not trained "
+			    "(PORTSC 0x%x, link state %d%s); warm reset", port,
+			    raw, XHCI_PS_PLS_GET(raw),
+			    (raw & XHCI_PS_CAS) ? ", cold attach" : "");
+			reg |= XHCI_PS_WPR;
+		} else {
+			reg |= XHCI_PS_PR;
+		}
 		break;
 	case CFS_PORT_POWER:
 		reg |= XHCI_PS_PP;
@@ -471,7 +507,8 @@
 	}
 
 	ps = cs = 0;
-	if (reg & XHCI_PS_CCS)
+	/* a link that needs a warm reset counts as connected; see above */
+	if ((reg & XHCI_PS_CCS) || xhci_port_needs_warm_reset(reg))
 		ps |= PORT_STATUS_CCS;
 	if (reg & XHCI_PS_PED)
 		ps |= PORT_STATUS_PES;
